														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2712857">
									

<p>That journal really weighs the piece down. It's a rote character sketch of an individual combining two tropes the wiki already has far too many examples of: the angry, petulant artist with nothing meaningful to say who replaces talent with anomalies; and the idiot who somehow acquires magical powers which he immediately proves too stupid to use and accidentally kills himself. Adrian even manages to be a completely overblown version of these characters - the French stuff and the 'there's no rule against magic' line are ridiculously over the top. It doesn't add anything to the article, destroys the mystery, and makes us sit through a cliched stock character rambling in a really annoying fashion.</p>
<p>The final note's particularly bad. It's like finding a dead man trapped under the wheel of his car in the garage and then finding a note on the table saying 'Hey honey I've gone out to fixed the car - I know you said I should replace our old wheel jack, but I'm sure it'll be fine!' It explains, in a completely inorganic fashion, exactly the specifics of the death and nothing else, and so comes off as contrived.</p>

